# Third-party material is stored byte for byte (ADR-039).
#
# assets/pieces/LICENSE.txt records a sha1 for each of the 12 SVG originals, and
# assets/fonts/LICENSE.txt is a byte-for-byte copy of the LICENSE from the DejaVu
# archive. With core.autocrlf=true - the usual setting on Windows - a checkout
# rewrites line endings, and both of those claims stop being true of the file on
# disk.
#
# -text stops git from rewriting line endings, on checkin and on checkout. That is
# all it does: it does not disable content filters (ident, clean/smudge), which
# would change the bytes just as effectively. None are configured here, and none
# may be configured for these paths.
#
# -text is not "binary": these files stay readable in a diff.
#
# Removing a line from this file silently breaks a claim made in another file.
assets/pieces/svg/*.svg    -text
assets/fonts/LICENSE.txt   -text

# PNG and TTF have no line endings to convert. Git works that out on its own, but
# by sniffing the first bytes of the file - a heuristic, not a guarantee. Say it.
*.png   binary
*.ttf   binary
